      "id": 1,
      "text": "Judsonia was founded in 1840 and named after Adoniram Judson, the first American missionary to Burma, reflecting its early Baptist roots.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 2"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.trawellino.com/destinations/united-states/arkansas_judsonia"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Before becoming Judsonia, the town was called Prospect Bluff and was established by Erastus Gregory in 1840.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        2
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Judsonia%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The book 'That's Judsonia' by William Ewing Orr, published in 1957, is considered the most complete history of the community.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        7
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://judsoniaar.weebly.com/about.html"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Judsonia sits just north of the Little Red River before it turns southeast toward the White River, northeast of Searcy.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
